  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The camera has exposure controls on it, but the thing is, once you're in VR and your eyes have *adjusted* to a dark world, there's no way to know that those exposure controls are *necessary*; everything still looks fine to you in the moment, until you see the photo on your PC later and it needs so much brightening to be visible that the whole thing is full of banding.\n\nIdeally I'd love to fix this by having 16bpc/48bpp photos, so we could adjust the exposure after the fact without banding, but if that's not feasible for some reason, another solution could be to have a visible histogram on the camera, so we could have a frame of reference to *know* when we need to crank up the exposure?  (It could just update once a second or so, if that seems like a threat to performance.)",
